# Conventions

## Imports and types

- Prefer `@/...` path alias (`src/*`).
- Domain types live in `src/data/interfaces/<domain>`.

## Services and contexts

- Services: one class per domain (e.g. `TicketService`) with `HttpClient` and `switch` on `HttpStatusCode`.
- Contexts expose actions (`Create`, `Edit`, `List`, `Delete`, …), loading/error state, and toasts via `useToast`.
- Prefer reusing existing services/contexts over duplicating HTTP calls in components.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — status handling scattered in UI
if (res.status !== 201) alert('fail');

// ✅ GOOD — service maps status, context shows toast
case HttpStatusCode.created:
  return body! as ITicket;
```

## Pages and forms

- Functional components; wrap pages with domain providers when needed.
- Forms: `react-hook-form`.
- Common page shape: lazy `list` + `form` inside modal/shell components.

## Do not introduce without request

- No Redux, Zustand, or React Query by default — stick to contexts/hooks already in the repo.

## Tooling

- Use project scripts from `package.json` (Vite, ESLint, Prettier, Cypress).
- Never commit `.env` or `VITE_*` secrets.
